cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, cite the ZeeBeam manuscript for the result and this repository for the programme record."
title: "Dark Lantern: Zero-Knowledge Light, Shuttered by Design (programme record)"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Hynes
    given-names: Cathal Ryan
    affiliation: PolieBotics
repository-code: "https://github.com/poliebotics/dark-lantern"
license-url: "https://github.com/poliebotics/dark-lantern/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Dark Lantern is the privacy and zero-knowledge research programme whose core result is ZeeBeam
  (github.com/poliebotics/zeebeam). This repository is a curated public subset of the programme record beyond
  ZeeBeam: selected standalone proof outputs, diagnostics, notes, audit prompts and verdicts, and retained fixtures.
  Publication-subset notices identify omitted and non-rebuildable material. Historical notes are published as such;
  the ZeeBeam manuscript controls every current claim.
keywords:
  - Dark Lantern
  - ZeeBeam
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - projector-camera capture
  - execution binding
notes: "Drafted, built, proved and verified with BOSUN, the project's automated research assistant, under the principal's direction."
